        <item>
            <title>0.91</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:19:45 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791684701</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.91</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Addy can now record content-free session replays: layout, focus, agent states, clicks, overlays and activity counts. It never records text, keystroke characters, paths, titles or commands. Chunks are compressed and uploaded in the background so you can keep working.</li>
<li>Replays now include the pointer path. The pointer is sampled at up to 15 times per second, only while it moves and Addy is the active app. This doesn&#x27;t change hover behavior in any view.</li>
<li>Telemetry batches now carry a session ID, so telemetry can be matched to the replay from the same app launch. Shortcut use and incident marks appear in the replay as events with no properties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Setting ADDY_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 now turns off session replay along with telemetry.</li>
<li>Replays can be switched off remotely. If the server answers that recording is off, Addy stops recording and deletes any pending replay chunks.</li>
<li>A replay left behind by a crash or force quit is closed out on the next launch, so it still ends cleanly.</li>
<li>Setting ADDY_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT points telemetry and replay uploads at a local server for development.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Internal Changes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Replay and telemetry uploads now share one authentication path.</li>
<li>Added test coverage for replay encoding, keyframes, live upload, main-thread safety, pointer sampling and the remote off switch.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
